      "line": null,
      "code": "br->read_crc16 = FLAC__crc16_update_words32(br->buffer + br->crc16_offset, br->consumed_words - br->crc16_offset, br->read_crc16);",
      "note": "Missing wraparound guard. This bulk CRC call assumes `consumed_words >= crc16_offset`, but `FLAC__bitreader_clear()` can zero `consumed_words` without resetting `crc16_offset`. When the current resync scan later consumes only a smaller number of words, the unsigned subtraction underflows and the CRC helper reads out of bounds. The fix adds the missing predicate `if (br->consumed_words > br->crc16_offset)` around this call.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
